🛒 Retail Sales Analysis

End-to-end retail analytics project covering data quality, cleaning, validation, exploratory analysis, financial performance, customer behavior, category performance, and business recommendations.

📌 Project Overview

This project analyzes retail transaction data to understand sales performance, profitability, customer behavior, product-category performance, and time-based sales patterns.

The workflow starts with raw transactional data and moves through:

Data inspection and auditing

Missing-value analysis

Data cleaning and validation

Feature engineering

Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)

Financial and profitability analysis

Customer segmentation and purchase-frequency analysis

Category and demographic analysis

Time-based performance analysis

Business insights and strategic recommendations

The supplied analysis reports 1,987 usable transactions across a two-year period (2022–2023), 3 product categories, and 155 customers.

🎯 Business Problem

Retail businesses need to understand not only how much they sell, but also where revenue and profit come from, who their customers are, and when demand is strongest.

This project addresses questions such as:

Which product categories generate the most revenue?

Which categories provide the strongest profitability and margins?

How large is the average customer order?

Which customer age groups contribute the most revenue?

Are there meaningful differences in purchasing behavior by gender?

Which age × category combinations are the most valuable?

Which days and months generate the highest sales?

How frequently do customers purchase?

Which customer segments should receive greater marketing attention?

How can sales, promotions, inventory, and loyalty strategies be improved?

