💡 Key Business Insights

1. Electronics is the main revenue engine

Electronics contributes the highest category revenue and is particularly important among older customer segments.

2. Beauty has strong economic value

Beauty has the highest reported AOV and gross margin, making it a strong candidate for cross-selling and margin-focused promotions.

3. Clothing drives transaction volume

Clothing has the highest units-per-order figure and is the strongest category for the 25–34 segment.

4. Customer preferences vary by age

Different age groups show distinct category preferences, creating opportunities for targeted recommendations.

5. Sunday is the strongest shopping day

The large difference between Sunday and Tuesday revenue suggests that promotions and staffing can be optimized by day of week.

6. Q4 is strategically important

October–December shows strong performance, with December identified as the strongest month in the final analysis.

7. Customer retention appears strong

The analysis reports a 100% repeat-customer rate and several highly frequent customers, supporting loyalty and VIP strategies.

🎯 Strategic Recommendations

1. Target High-Value Segments

Prioritize 25–34 × Clothing campaigns.

Use targeted campaigns for the 18–24 segment, which has the highest reported AOV.

Develop personalized recommendations by age group.

2. Leverage Category Strengths

Maintain strong Electronics inventory, especially during peak periods.

Promote Beauty as a higher-margin cross-sell opportunity.

Use Clothing as a high-volume acquisition and cross-selling category.

3. Optimize Promotions by Time

Use Sunday and weekend promotions to capitalize on stronger demand.

Test Tuesday-specific promotions to improve weak-day performance.

Increase inventory and marketing preparation before the Q4 peak.

4. Improve Customer Personalization

Use age × category preferences for product recommendations.

Develop targeted campaigns for female and male category preferences.

Personalize offers using previous purchase behavior.

5. Build Loyalty Programs

Create VIP benefits for highly frequent customers.

Reward repeat purchasing and higher customer lifetime value.

Use purchase history to develop personalized offers.

🧪 Validation & Data Quality

The analysis includes explicit validation of key business rules.

The cleaned dataset is reported to satisfy:

Positive quantity values

Positive selling prices

Non-negative COGS and sales values

Sales consistency with quantity × price_per_unit

Unique transaction identifiers in the retained transaction-level dataset

This validation step helps establish the cleaned dataset as the analytical source of truth.

▶️ How to Run the Project

1. Clone the repository

git clone <your-repository-url>
cd <your-repository-folder>

2. Create a virtual environment

python -m venv .venv

Activate it:

Windows

.venv\Scripts\activate

macOS / Linux

source .venv/bin/activate

3. Install dependencies

pip install pandas numpy matplotlib seaborn jupyter

4. Start Jupyter Notebook

jupyter notebook

5. Run the analysis

Open the project notebook and execute the cells from top to bottom.

Make sure the raw CSV path used by the notebook matches the location of your dataset.

