⚠️ Important Notes

The analysis is based on the supplied historical retail transaction dataset.

Reported financial figures describe the analyzed observation period and should not automatically be interpreted as annualized figures.

Business recommendations are derived from the observed patterns in the dataset.

The README does not assume additional SQL or Power BI functionality unless those files are present in the repository.

📌 Conclusion

This project demonstrates how raw retail transaction data can be transformed into actionable business intelligence through a structured analytics workflow.

The analysis shows a business with:

$908K+ reported revenue

79.2% reported gross margin

Strong category-level differentiation

Distinct customer preferences by age and gender

Significant day- and month-level seasonality

High reported repeat-purchase activity

Clear opportunities for targeted marketing, cross-selling, loyalty programs, and demand-based planning

The overall objective is to move beyond descriptive reporting and use data to support better commercial, customer, and operational decisions.

